            <!-- 1. ERD -->
            <section class="content-section" id="erd">
                <h2>Master Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD)</h2>
                <p>
                    Software Asset Management bridges two divergent domains: <strong>physical technical reality</strong> (file systems, processes, clusters, and registry entries discovered on IT infrastructure) and <strong>financial contractual reality</strong> (procurement purchase orders, enterprise agreements, licensing metrics, and maintenance terms).
                </p>
                <p>
                    The <strong>Software Model (<code>cmdb_software_product_model</code>)</strong> serves as the indispensable relational bridge. Discovered installations cluster into normalized Discovery Models that link to the Software Model. In parallel, procurement purchase orders generate Software Entitlements that also reference the Software Model, allowing the 7-step Reconciliation Engine to compute mathematical compliance.
                </p>

                <div class="diagram-block" style="margin: 28px 0;">
                    <div class="diagram-title">End-to-End SAM Pro Relational Architecture &amp; Data Flow</div>
                    <div class="mermaid">
                    graph TD
                        subgraph DiscoveryLayer["Layer 1: Discovery, Normalization and Usage"]
                            INSTALL["Software Installs<br/>(cmdb_sam_sw_install)"] -->|Cluster / Hash| DISCO["Discovery Models<br/>(cmdb_sam_sw_discovery_model)"]
                            USAGE["Software Usage<br/>(cmdb_sam_sw_usage)"] -->|Metering Data| INSTALL
                            CUSTOM_NORM["Custom Norm Rules<br/>(samp_custom_normalization_rule)"] -.->|Override| DISCO
                        end

                        subgraph ModelingLayer["Layer 2: Modeling, Content and Lifecycles"]
                            DISCO -->|Maps via DMAP| MODEL["Software Product Models<br/>(cmdb_software_product_model)"]
                            PPN["Publisher Part Numbers<br/>(samp_sw_publisher_part_number)"] -->|Populates| MODEL
                            DMAP["Discovery Maps<br/>(samp_sw_entitlement_definition)"] -->|Defines Logic| MODEL
                            LIFE["Lifecycle Milestones<br/>(samp_sw_lifecycle)"] -->|Enriches Dates| MODEL
                            SUITE["Suite Components<br/>(cmdb_software_component_model)"] -->|Inferred Parent| MODEL
                        end

                        subgraph EntitlementLayer["Layer 3: Financial Entitlements and Allocations"]
                            PO["Purchase Orders<br/>(proc_po)"] -->|Procures| ENT["Software Entitlements<br/>(alm_license)"]
                            ENT -->|Entitles Model| MODEL
                            ENT -->|Allocate User| USER_ALLOC["User Allocations<br/>(alm_entitlement_user)"]
                            ENT -->|Allocate Device| ASSET_ALLOC["Device Allocations<br/>(alm_entitlement_asset)"]
                            SAAS["SaaS Subscriptions<br/>(samp_sw_subscription)"] -->|Cloud Rights| MODEL
                        end

                        subgraph ReconciliationLayer["Layer 4: Reconciliation, ELP and Remediation"]
                            MODEL -->|Evaluates| RECON_RUN["Reconciliation Runs<br/>(samp_reconciliation_result)"]
                            RECON_RUN -->|Granular ELP| METRIC_RES["License Metric Results<br/>(samp_license_metric_result)"]
                            METRIC_RES -->|Generates on Deficit| REMED["Remediation Options<br/>(samp_remediation_option)"]
                            METRIC_RES -->|Flags| UNLIC["Unlicensed Installs<br/>(samp_sw_unlicensed_install)"]
                        end

                        subgraph ReclamationLayer["Layer 5: Continuous Optimization and Harvesting"]
                            MODEL -->|Governs| RECL_RULE["Reclamation Rules<br/>(samp_sw_reclamation_rule)"]
                            USAGE -->|Inactivity Evaluation| RECL_CAND["Reclamation Candidates<br/>(samp_sw_reclamation_candidate)"]
                            RECL_RULE -->|Triggers Workflow| RECL_CAND
                            RECL_CAND -->|Zero-Touch Client| CSD["Client Software Distribution<br/>(SCCM / Jamf Uninstall)"]
                        end

                        classDef default fill:#161b26,stroke:#334155,stroke-width:1px,color:#f8fafc
                        classDef highlight fill:#161b26,stroke:#10b981,stroke-width:2px,color:#f8fafc
                        classDef blue fill:#161b26,stroke:#3b82f6,stroke-width:2px,color:#f8fafc
                        classDef amber fill:#161b26,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px,color:#f8fafc
                        classDef purple fill:#161b26,stroke:#8b5cf6,stroke-width:2px,color:#f8fafc

                        class MODEL,ENT highlight
                        class DISCO,INSTALL blue
                        class METRIC_RES,REMED amber
                        class RECL_CAND,SAAS purple
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="info-card info-card--important">
                    <div class="info-card-title">Inheritance &amp; Scoping Foundations</div>
                    <p>
                        Understanding database inheritance is foundational for ServiceNow technical architects and developers:
                    </p>
                    <ul class="feature-bullet-list">
                        <li><strong><code>alm_license</code> extends <code>alm_asset</code>:</strong> Because entitlements inherit base asset tables, they automatically gain asset depreciation schedules, capital expense accounting, asset tags, cost centers, and vendor company linkages.</li>
                        <li><strong><code>cmdb_software_product_model</code> extends <code>cmdb_model</code>:</strong> Inherits product catalog properties, allowing software models to be published into the Service Catalog for user request fulfillment.</li>
                        <li><strong><code>cmdb_sam_sw_install</code> extends <code>cmdb_ci</code>:</strong> Enables installs to participate in CMDB relationship queries, CI lifecycle status auditing, and Identification and Reconciliation Engine (IRE) deduplication.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </section>

